gar/data/1993004/000199300426000050/0001993004-26-000050-index.htm","accession":"0001993004-26-000050"},{"text":"Growth has been positive in 7 of the last 8 year-on-year comparisons, so this is a trend rather than one good quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1993004/000199300426000050/0001993004-26-000050-index.htm","accession":"0001993004-26-000050"},{"text":"Operating cash flow is positive at $688.2m over the trailing year, so the business funds itself and is not dependent on raising money.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1993004/000199300426000029/0001993004-26-000029-index.htm","accession":"0001993004-26-000029"},{"text":"Share count is close to flat (0.5% over the year), so growth in the business accrues to existing holders rather than being diluted away.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1993004/000199300426000050/0001993004-26-000050-index.htm","accession":"0001993004-26-000050"}],"bear":[{"text":"Debt of $3.5bn against equity of $2.9bn. Leverage decides who controls the outcome if trading deteriorates, and it is not the shareholder.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1993004/000199300426000050/0001993004-26-000050-index.htm","accession":"0001993004-26-000050"},{"text":"Officers and directors hold only 0.2% of the shares. There is little alignment between what happens to the share price and what happens to them.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1993004/000163440326000006/0001634403-26-000006-index.htm"},{"text":"Base rate: 57.8% of US common stocks underperformed one-month Treasury bills over their lifetimes (Bessembinder, Journal of Financial Economics, 2018). Nothing above changes that starting point.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2018.06.004"}],"triggers":[{"id":"growth_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Revenue growth falls below 0.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"revenue_growth_yoy","comparison":"below","threshold":0.0